1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:01,734
Mara is still looking at you.

2
00:00:01,734 --> 00:00:02,389
Behind her,

3
00:00:02,389 --> 00:00:04,848
the shelves rattle against the wall.

4
00:00:04,848 --> 00:00:06,981
The crack in the window gives a small tick,

5
00:00:06,981 --> 00:00:08,959
like a clock making up its mind.

6
00:00:08,959 --> 00:00:10,958
Day 31 starts with a choice

7
00:00:10,958 --> 00:00:13,533
you don't get long to think about.

8
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:14,658
You can stay and find

9
00:00:14,658 --> 00:00:16,442
out what the shaking is for.

10
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:17,974
Or you can take the

11
00:00:17,974 --> 00:00:19,441
only door they've left you.

12
00:00:19,441 --> 00:00:21,857
You put the tin you caught into your bag.

13
00:00:21,857 --> 00:00:24,091
Leaving it on the floor feels rude.

14
00:00:24,091 --> 00:00:26,648
Then you lift the bag by its handle.

15
00:00:26,648 --> 00:00:28,168
That's your answer.

16
00:00:28,168 --> 00:00:29,487
Mara nods once,

17
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:32,241
as if you've said something sensible.

18
00:00:32,241 --> 00:00:34,007
You walk out under the canopy.

19
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:35,924
The striped figure is

20
00:00:35,924 --> 00:00:37,252
standing by the pumps.

21
00:00:37,252 --> 00:00:38,883
Its scanner rises.

22
00:00:38,883 --> 00:00:41,508
The pale line comes across the forecourt,

23
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:44,133
and for the first time in thirty days,

24
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:45,937
it touches you directly.

25
00:00:46,472 --> 00:00:47,942
It crosses your shoes,

26
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:50,416
your bag, the scarf at your neck.

27
00:00:51,048 --> 00:00:52,504
You feel nothing.

28
00:00:52,504 --> 00:00:54,283
Somehow, that's worse.

29
00:00:54,283 --> 00:00:57,402
The line moves to Mara, then away.

30
00:00:57,402 --> 00:00:59,131
Nobody follows you.

31
00:00:59,131 --> 00:01:00,720
The plain figure doesn't

32
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:02,931
even look up from its case.

33
00:01:02,931 --> 00:01:04,495
You walk past the small craft

34
00:01:04,495 --> 00:01:06,048
without looking at it,

35
00:01:06,048 --> 00:01:08,006
which takes more effort than walking.

36
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:09,139
Then you step through

37
00:01:09,139 --> 00:01:10,909
the gap in the boundary.

38
00:01:10,909 --> 00:01:11,857
Behind you,

39
00:01:11,857 --> 00:01:15,805
there's a soft sound, like a page being turned.

40
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:18,392
When you look back, the gap is gone.

41
00:01:18,392 --> 00:01:20,729
The light is whole again,

42
00:01:20,729 --> 00:01:22,639
with the station inside it.

43
00:01:22,639 --> 00:01:24,004
The cracked window.

44
00:01:24,004 --> 00:01:24,983
The red can.

45
00:01:24,983 --> 00:01:26,392
The staff room where

46
00:01:26,392 --> 00:01:28,302
you stopped being safe.

47
00:01:28,741 --> 00:01:31,439
You couldn't go back now if you wanted to.

48
00:01:31,439 --> 00:01:34,602
You aren't sure yet whether you want to.

49
00:01:34,602 --> 00:01:36,689
Ahead, the joined circles keep

50
00:01:36,689 --> 00:01:38,806
lighting along the roadside path.

51
00:01:38,806 --> 00:01:41,204
When you stop, they wait.

52
00:01:41,204 --> 00:01:44,118
When you walk, the next one glows.

53
00:01:44,492 --> 00:01:46,982
It feels less like a road and more like a

54
00:01:46,982 --> 00:01:49,971
hallway somebody has switched on for you.

55
00:01:49,971 --> 00:01:52,399
At the bend, the dark units are

56
00:01:52,399 --> 00:01:54,629
exactly where they were on day 18.

57
00:01:55,163 --> 00:01:56,706
Taller than you.

58
00:01:56,706 --> 00:01:57,432
Smooth.

59
00:01:57,432 --> 00:01:58,640
No faces.

60
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:01,500
Joined circles glowing near their base.

61
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,426
The light runs on between them,

62
00:02:03,426 --> 00:02:06,102
toward a part of the city you've never seen.

63
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:08,055
Mara stops beside you,

64
00:02:08,055 --> 00:02:10,105
at the crease on your map that marks

65
00:02:10,105 --> 00:02:12,472
the farthest you have ever gone.

66
00:02:12,472 --> 00:02:13,719
She asks the question

67
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:15,816
you've both been avoiding.

68
00:02:15,816 --> 00:02:16,915
Do you follow it?

69
00:02:16,915 --> 00:02:18,625
You tell her the only thing

70
00:02:18,625 --> 00:02:20,708
thirty days have taught you for certain.

71
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:23,580
If they built it, you don't understand it.

72
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,189
So you step off the road.

73
00:02:25,189 --> 00:02:26,117
Down the bank,

74
00:02:26,117 --> 00:02:29,474
into the long grass, behind the fence of a field.

75
00:02:29,474 --> 00:02:31,388
The next circle stays dark.

76
00:02:31,793 --> 00:02:34,139
Behind you, the lit ones fade,

77
00:02:34,139 --> 00:02:36,853
one by one, back toward the bend.

78
00:02:36,853 --> 00:02:39,437
As if the road has stopped expecting you.

79
00:02:40,228 --> 00:02:42,131
You don't know whether that's freedom,

80
00:02:42,131 --> 00:02:43,032
or whether you've

81
00:02:43,032 --> 00:02:45,555
just made yourself harder to find.

82
00:02:45,555 --> 00:02:47,362
That night, you sleep in a

83
00:02:47,362 --> 00:02:50,522
concrete drain that runs under the road.

84
00:02:50,522 --> 00:02:51,689
It's round,

85
00:02:51,689 --> 00:02:54,475
cold, and just tall enough to sit up in,

86
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:57,159
if you don't mind hitting your head.

87
00:02:57,159 --> 00:02:58,114
You do mind.

88
00:02:58,114 --> 00:03:00,212
You do it twice anyway.

89
00:03:00,212 --> 00:03:01,692
A thin trickle of water

90
00:03:01,692 --> 00:03:03,601
runs down the middle,

91
00:03:03,601 --> 00:03:06,328
and you and Mara each take a dry ledge.

92
00:03:06,328 --> 00:03:08,441
You use the flashlight for

93
00:03:08,441 --> 00:03:10,014
one minute to check the bags.

94
00:03:10,014 --> 00:03:12,486
The beam is weaker than yesterday.

95
00:03:12,486 --> 00:03:14,740
You open the tin and write:

96
00:03:15,434 --> 00:03:16,551
under the road.

97
00:03:16,551 --> 00:03:16,970
Then,

98
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:22,659
because you've learned something, you add a question mark.

99
00:03:22,659 --> 00:03:23,706
On day 33,

100
00:03:23,706 --> 00:03:26,289
you find out who the road is for.

101
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:27,501
For two days,

102
00:03:27,858 --> 00:03:30,413
you've watched it from the mouth of the drain.

103
00:03:30,413 --> 00:03:32,220
The units barely move.

104
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,071
Once, one slides a short way

105
00:03:34,071 --> 00:03:36,638
sideways and back onto its mark,

106
00:03:36,638 --> 00:03:38,580
without legs and without a sound,

107
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:41,317
the way the small craft landed without wheels.

108
00:03:41,317 --> 00:03:42,837
You test the road the way

109
00:03:42,837 --> 00:03:45,169
you used to test the forecourt.

110
00:03:45,169 --> 00:03:46,904
With something that isn't you.

111
00:03:46,904 --> 00:03:49,313
You eat what's inside the tin you

112
00:03:49,313 --> 00:03:51,341
caught on day 30, and Mara rolls the

113
00:03:51,341 --> 00:03:53,940
empty tin up the bank onto the road.

114
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:56,462
It clatters to a stop between two units.

115
00:03:56,804 --> 00:03:57,827
Nothing lights.

116
00:03:57,827 --> 00:03:58,979
In the afternoon,

117
00:03:58,979 --> 00:04:02,026
a man comes walking from the direction of the bend.

118
00:04:02,026 --> 00:04:04,290
He's pulling a wheeled suitcase.

119
00:04:04,290 --> 00:04:05,154
Every few steps,

120
00:04:05,154 --> 00:04:07,128
the circles ahead of him glow,

121
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:10,214
one unit at a time, showing him the way.

122
00:04:10,214 --> 00:04:11,825
He isn't hiding.

123
00:04:11,825 --> 00:04:12,935
He isn't running.

124
00:04:12,935 --> 00:04:14,669
He looks relieved.

125
00:04:14,669 --> 00:04:15,691
Mara half rises.

126
00:04:15,691 --> 00:04:18,214
You can see the words getting ready.

127
00:04:18,734 --> 00:04:19,855
Then she asks you,

128
00:04:19,855 --> 00:04:22,456
very quietly, what she would tell him.

129
00:04:23,072 --> 00:04:24,164
You think about it.

130
00:04:24,164 --> 00:04:26,483
That the scanner goes through walls.

131
00:04:26,936 --> 00:04:29,536
That nobody you know of has been hurt.

132
00:04:29,536 --> 00:04:32,954
That you have no idea where the road goes.

133
00:04:32,954 --> 00:04:35,414
Everything you know would just make

134
00:04:35,414 --> 00:04:37,973
him stand in the road and be frightened.

135
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,628
So neither of you calls out.

136
00:04:40,628 --> 00:04:42,542
The suitcase wheels rattle

137
00:04:42,542 --> 00:04:44,419
along the road above your heads.

138
00:04:44,419 --> 00:04:47,279
The lights lead him around the next curve.

139
00:04:47,279 --> 00:04:49,399
You never see him again.

140
00:04:49,933 --> 00:04:50,688
That evening,

141
00:04:50,688 --> 00:04:54,010
Mara takes the pencil and writes in the ledger herself.

142
00:04:54,593 --> 00:04:56,468
The road lights for people.

143
00:04:56,468 --> 00:04:57,673
Not for tins.

144
00:04:58,369 --> 00:05:01,964
Underneath, smaller: we didn't call out.

145
00:05:02,451 --> 00:05:05,356
You don't argue with either line.

146
00:05:05,356 --> 00:05:06,388
By day 35,

147
00:05:06,388 --> 00:05:08,473
you can see the bottom of both bags.

148
00:05:08,473 --> 00:05:10,801
You don't count the drinks anymore.

149
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,827
You know the number is small,

150
00:05:12,827 --> 00:05:15,806
and saying it out loud won't make it bigger.

151
00:05:15,806 --> 00:05:17,671
Across the field behind the drain,

152
00:05:17,671 --> 00:05:20,519
there's a low building with a fenced garden yard.

153
00:05:20,519 --> 00:05:21,825
A hardware store.

154
00:05:22,455 --> 00:05:24,029
You've been looking at it for days,

155
00:05:24,029 --> 00:05:25,289
the way you used to look at

156
00:05:25,289 --> 00:05:27,843
the shelves by the station window.

157
00:05:27,843 --> 00:05:30,665
Useful, and in plain view.

158
00:05:30,665 --> 00:05:33,723
You go at dusk, along the fence line.

159
00:05:33,723 --> 00:05:36,416
One watches while the other moves,

160
00:05:36,416 --> 00:05:37,828
the way you did on day three.

161
00:05:37,828 --> 00:05:39,539
The shutter is half open.

162
00:05:39,864 --> 00:05:41,839
Somebody has been here before you.

163
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:43,549
The water aisle is bare.

164
00:05:43,875 --> 00:05:45,309
So is anything with the

165
00:05:45,309 --> 00:05:47,402
word emergency printed on it.

166
00:05:47,857 --> 00:05:49,154
What's left are the

167
00:05:49,154 --> 00:05:51,529
things nobody grabs in a panic.

168
00:05:51,871 --> 00:05:53,393
You find batteries.

169
00:05:53,393 --> 00:05:55,067
Every size except the

170
00:05:55,067 --> 00:05:56,924
one your flashlight takes.

171
00:05:56,924 --> 00:05:58,336
You check twice.

172
00:05:58,774 --> 00:06:00,273
The flashlight flickers,

173
00:06:00,273 --> 00:06:02,671
as if it's taking this personally.

174
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:04,547
In the camping aisle,

175
00:06:04,547 --> 00:06:07,863
Mara finds a wind-up lantern, still in its box.

176
00:06:07,863 --> 00:06:10,270
Forty turns of the handle buys a few

177
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:12,765
minutes of light, and a whirring sound

178
00:06:12,765 --> 00:06:16,442
like a very small, very determined insect.

179
00:06:16,442 --> 00:06:18,057
You take it.

180
00:06:18,057 --> 00:06:20,088
You also take a folded tarp,

181
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:23,064
two clean buckets, a roll of tape,

182
00:06:23,064 --> 00:06:26,635
a small camping stove, and three gas canisters.

183
00:06:26,635 --> 00:06:29,328
Then you remember the plain figure

184
00:06:29,328 --> 00:06:31,500
touching the gap on the station shelf.

185
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:34,555
So you spend twenty minutes spreading out what's left,

186
00:06:34,555 --> 00:06:36,563
until nothing looks missing.

187
00:06:37,016 --> 00:06:38,444
It's the first time you've

188
00:06:38,444 --> 00:06:40,349
ever tidied a shop on your way out.

189
00:06:40,349 --> 00:06:42,831
You sleep in the storeroom at the back,

190
00:06:42,831 --> 00:06:43,799
between a workbench

191
00:06:43,799 --> 00:06:45,552
and a stack of empty pallets.

192
00:06:45,909 --> 00:06:47,960
On day 37, it rains.

193
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:50,086
You have never been this

194
00:06:50,086 --> 00:06:51,575
happy to see bad weather.

195
00:06:51,575 --> 00:06:53,745
You tie the tarp between two posts of

196
00:06:53,745 --> 00:06:55,177
the garden yard fence,

197
00:06:55,177 --> 00:06:58,641
lower at one corner, and set the buckets underneath.

198
00:06:58,641 --> 00:07:01,191
The rain drums on the plastic all night.

199
00:07:01,532 --> 00:07:02,228
By morning,

200
00:07:02,228 --> 00:07:05,383
both buckets are full of gray water and bits of leaf.

201
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:06,648
Mara won't let either

202
00:07:06,648 --> 00:07:08,501
of you drink it like that.

203
00:07:08,826 --> 00:07:10,485
You set the stove up just inside

204
00:07:10,485 --> 00:07:12,296
the open back door of the storeroom

205
00:07:12,296 --> 00:07:14,887
and boil the water one pot at a time.

206
00:07:14,887 --> 00:07:17,930
The gas runs down faster than you hoped.

207
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:21,127
By noon, every empty bottle in both

208
00:07:21,127 --> 00:07:23,303
bags is full again, and still warm.

209
00:07:23,303 --> 00:07:24,891
You write the new

210
00:07:24,891 --> 00:07:26,318
number on the receipt roll.

211
00:07:26,318 --> 00:07:27,796
For the first time in weeks,

212
00:07:27,796 --> 00:07:28,861
it's going up.

213
00:07:29,332 --> 00:07:31,534
The store has a roof, a back door,

214
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:34,485
and a whole field between you and the road.

215
00:07:34,485 --> 00:07:35,919
Staying seems obvious.

216
00:07:35,919 --> 00:07:37,900
You've thought that before.

217
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:39,913
You write it down anyway.

218
00:07:39,913 --> 00:07:41,273
Stay, for now.

219
00:07:41,273 --> 00:07:44,131
Mara reads it and underlines for now.

220
00:07:44,762 --> 00:07:45,407
On day 40,

221
00:07:45,407 --> 00:07:48,113
the plain figure walks out of the field.

222
00:07:48,455 --> 00:07:49,605
Not from the road.

223
00:07:49,605 --> 00:07:50,573
From the field,

224
00:07:50,573 --> 00:07:53,142
along the same fence line you use.

225
00:07:53,142 --> 00:07:54,154
You watch through a

226
00:07:54,154 --> 00:07:55,520
gap in the storeroom door.

227
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,587
It doesn't go to the shelves.

228
00:07:57,587 --> 00:07:59,660
You filled every gap on those shelves.

229
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,859
It goes straight to the garden

230
00:08:01,859 --> 00:08:03,632
yard and stands under the tarp.

231
00:08:03,632 --> 00:08:05,011
You hid everything you

232
00:08:05,011 --> 00:08:06,502
took from inside the store.

233
00:08:06,502 --> 00:08:08,207
Then you hung the biggest thing

234
00:08:08,207 --> 00:08:10,647
you took outside, to catch the sky.

235
00:08:10,647 --> 00:08:13,487
It touches the tarp with one gloved hand.

236
00:08:13,487 --> 00:08:15,109
On the fence post beside it,

237
00:08:15,109 --> 00:08:16,415
it leaves a mark.

238
00:08:16,901 --> 00:08:18,304
A vertical line with a

239
00:08:18,304 --> 00:08:19,767
short stroke across it.

240
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:21,516
The same mark it left

241
00:08:21,516 --> 00:08:22,750
under the station shelf.

242
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,860
Then the striped figure arrives.

243
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:25,858
The scanner rises.

244
00:08:25,858 --> 00:08:26,909
The pale line comes

245
00:08:26,909 --> 00:08:29,097
straight through the storeroom wall.

246
00:08:29,097 --> 00:08:31,175
It crosses the workbench,

247
00:08:31,175 --> 00:08:33,955
the stove, Mara's bag and yours.

248
00:08:33,955 --> 00:08:36,127
It stops on the receipt tin.

249
00:08:36,566 --> 00:08:37,745
And it waits.

250
00:08:37,745 --> 00:08:38,671
Six seconds.

251
00:08:38,671 --> 00:08:40,419
You count them,

252
00:08:40,419 --> 00:08:42,608
the way you counted them on day one.

253
00:08:42,608 --> 00:08:45,358
Then the line moves on, and they leave.

254
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:46,745
They don't take the tarp.

255
00:08:46,745 --> 00:08:48,304
They don't take the tin.

256
00:08:48,304 --> 00:08:49,160
That night,

257
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:54,078
with the lantern whirring, you read back through the roll.

258
00:08:54,078 --> 00:08:57,299
Day one, the scanner stopped at a bottle.

259
00:08:57,299 --> 00:08:59,410
The first supply run, a receipt.

260
00:08:59,410 --> 00:09:01,862
Day twelve, Mara's empty bag.

261
00:09:01,862 --> 00:09:03,500
Today, the tin.

262
00:09:04,116 --> 00:09:06,340
Every time, something you'd carried.

263
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:08,982
Never, as far as you know, on you.

264
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:11,357
Maybe it can't see you, you say.

265
00:09:11,779 --> 00:09:13,759
Maybe it sees what you touch.

266
00:09:13,759 --> 00:09:16,133
Mara says maybe it sees you just fine,

267
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:18,453
and finds your things more interesting.

268
00:09:18,811 --> 00:09:20,153
You write both down.

269
00:09:20,153 --> 00:09:21,048
Next to them,

270
00:09:21,048 --> 00:09:24,950
in capital letters, you write: theory.

271
00:09:24,950 --> 00:09:26,757
On day 42,

272
00:09:26,757 --> 00:09:29,021
Mara wants to see where the road goes.

273
00:09:29,021 --> 00:09:30,321
Not walk it.

274
00:09:30,321 --> 00:09:30,950
See it.

275
00:09:30,950 --> 00:09:33,596
She says she's tired of running

276
00:09:33,596 --> 00:09:35,776
from a place she's never looked at.

277
00:09:35,776 --> 00:09:38,786
You can't argue with that, so you don't.

278
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,211
A mile from the store,

279
00:09:40,211 --> 00:09:42,564
a footbridge crosses the highway.

280
00:09:42,564 --> 00:09:44,293
You climb it at dusk,

281
00:09:44,293 --> 00:09:47,481
low, on your knees for the last few steps.

282
00:09:47,481 --> 00:09:48,237
From the top,

283
00:09:48,237 --> 00:09:50,432
you can see the road from the bend.

284
00:09:50,432 --> 00:09:52,136
It joins the highway.

285
00:09:52,622 --> 00:09:55,152
The highway is lined with units too.

286
00:09:55,152 --> 00:09:58,109
Other lit roads join it from every direction,

287
00:09:58,109 --> 00:10:00,549
like threads pulled toward one point.

288
00:10:00,972 --> 00:10:02,611
That point is a stadium near the

289
00:10:02,611 --> 00:10:04,997
middle of the city, right under the ship.

290
00:10:05,532 --> 00:10:07,190
Its floodlights are dark,

291
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,166
but the whole bowl is glowing.

292
00:10:09,166 --> 00:10:10,725
Along every lit road,

293
00:10:10,725 --> 00:10:13,603
small figures are walking toward it.

294
00:10:13,978 --> 00:10:15,561
You can't see their faces.

295
00:10:15,561 --> 00:10:16,968
You can see the circles

296
00:10:16,968 --> 00:10:19,106
lighting up ahead of them.

297
00:10:19,106 --> 00:10:20,352
Some walk in pairs.

298
00:10:20,352 --> 00:10:21,712
Some walk alone.

299
00:10:22,102 --> 00:10:24,763
Some carry bags, the way you carry yours.

300
00:10:25,378 --> 00:10:27,167
Small craft settle into the

301
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:29,098
stadium and lift away again.

302
00:10:29,098 --> 00:10:30,772
You watch for an hour.

303
00:10:30,772 --> 00:10:33,280
You don't see anyone walk out.

304
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,980
On day 18, you thought the route

305
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:37,958
out of the city was being organized.

306
00:10:37,958 --> 00:10:39,596
You were half right.

307
00:10:39,596 --> 00:10:40,707
It's organized.

308
00:10:40,707 --> 00:10:42,026
It just isn't out.

309
00:10:42,026 --> 00:10:44,495
Mara says they're collecting people.

310
00:10:44,495 --> 00:10:47,014
You say maybe they're counting them.

311
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:48,945
You've spent 42 days

312
00:10:48,945 --> 00:10:50,871
counting everything you own.

313
00:10:50,871 --> 00:10:52,047
You don't like how

314
00:10:52,047 --> 00:10:53,535
easily you can picture it.

315
00:10:53,535 --> 00:10:55,048
Neither of you knows.

316
00:10:55,487 --> 00:10:56,421
On the way down,

317
00:10:56,421 --> 00:10:59,138
Mara's hands are shaking, and so are yours.

318
00:10:59,496 --> 00:11:01,640
Neither of you comments on that.

319
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,992
On day 45, you test the one theory

320
00:11:03,992 --> 00:11:06,644
you can test without testing yourselves.

321
00:11:06,644 --> 00:11:08,391
First, you copy the ledger.

322
00:11:08,391 --> 00:11:09,278
Not all of it.

323
00:11:09,278 --> 00:11:10,873
Just the lines that matter,

324
00:11:10,873 --> 00:11:13,736
in tiny handwriting, on the back of your map.

325
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:15,227
40 minutes.

326
00:11:15,227 --> 00:11:16,169
Closed room.

327
00:11:16,169 --> 00:11:17,763
Safe behind the wall.

328
00:11:17,763 --> 00:11:20,080
They notice what changes.

329
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,130
The road lights for people.

330
00:11:22,130 --> 00:11:22,716
Theory.

331
00:11:22,716 --> 00:11:24,373
Then you leave the receipt tin

332
00:11:24,373 --> 00:11:25,559
at the mouth of the drain,

333
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:27,708
where the fence line meets the road.

334
00:11:27,708 --> 00:11:29,181
Mara hates this.

335
00:11:29,181 --> 00:11:32,036
She says that tin is the only thing

336
00:11:32,036 --> 00:11:34,684
that remembers every mistake you've made.

337
00:11:35,026 --> 00:11:37,192
You say that's what makes it good bait.

338
00:11:37,192 --> 00:11:39,898
You watch from the roof of the store,

339
00:11:39,898 --> 00:11:41,386
flat on your stomachs.

340
00:11:41,386 --> 00:11:41,969
At dusk,

341
00:11:41,969 --> 00:11:44,889
the plain figure comes along the road.

342
00:11:44,889 --> 00:11:46,230
It lifts the tin.

343
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:48,832
It holds it for a long time.

344
00:11:48,832 --> 00:11:50,406
Then it sets it down

345
00:11:50,406 --> 00:11:52,646
exactly one step to the side.

346
00:11:52,646 --> 00:11:54,132
The way it moved the

347
00:11:54,132 --> 00:11:56,419
bicycle on your very first night.

348
00:11:56,419 --> 00:11:57,638
It places a marker

349
00:11:57,638 --> 00:11:59,539
beside it and walks away.

350
00:11:59,539 --> 00:12:00,845
You wait two hours

351
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,199
before you go and get it.

352
00:12:03,199 --> 00:12:05,198
Inside, the receipt roll is wound

353
00:12:05,198 --> 00:12:08,486
tighter and neater than you have ever managed.

354
00:12:08,486 --> 00:12:10,093
At the very end,

355
00:12:10,093 --> 00:12:13,350
under your last line, there's something new.

356
00:12:13,350 --> 00:12:16,029
Two circles, joined by a short line.

357
00:12:16,029 --> 00:12:18,374
Mara stares at it for a long time.

358
00:12:18,374 --> 00:12:20,385
Then she says out loud what

359
00:12:20,385 --> 00:12:23,234
you've both been circling for weeks.

360
00:12:23,234 --> 00:12:23,991
On day one,

361
00:12:23,991 --> 00:12:26,626
there were two of you at the station.

362
00:12:26,626 --> 00:12:28,189
You, in the shop.

363
00:12:28,627 --> 00:12:28,954
Her,

364
00:12:28,954 --> 00:12:31,703
somewhere close enough to watch you move.

365
00:12:31,703 --> 00:12:33,567
The first marker they

366
00:12:33,567 --> 00:12:34,926
ever placed was two circles.

367
00:12:34,926 --> 00:12:36,335
The gap in the boundary was

368
00:12:36,335 --> 00:12:37,822
wide enough for two people.

369
00:12:37,822 --> 00:12:39,791
You point out that every unit on

370
00:12:39,791 --> 00:12:41,756
the road has joined circles too.

371
00:12:41,756 --> 00:12:44,594
Then there are a lot of pairs, she says.

372
00:12:44,594 --> 00:12:46,159
You write her theory down.

373
00:12:46,159 --> 00:12:47,897
Under it, you write that your

374
00:12:47,897 --> 00:12:50,544
ledger now has a third author.

375
00:12:50,544 --> 00:12:52,556
On day 48, you wake to slow

376
00:12:52,556 --> 00:12:54,667
footsteps going around the store.

377
00:12:54,667 --> 00:12:57,192
The plain figure's case is open.

378
00:12:57,192 --> 00:12:58,883
Behind it, a narrow band of

379
00:12:58,883 --> 00:13:01,164
pale light stays on the ground.

380
00:13:01,164 --> 00:13:03,095
You've seen this before.

381
00:13:03,095 --> 00:13:04,013
Day 27.

382
00:13:04,436 --> 00:13:05,411
Three days later,

383
00:13:05,411 --> 00:13:09,594
the station shook, and the boundary opened toward their road.

384
00:13:09,594 --> 00:13:10,239
Last time,

385
00:13:10,239 --> 00:13:12,840
you waited, because you didn't know enough.

386
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,406
This time,

387
00:13:13,406 --> 00:13:15,486
you've seen where their roads lead.

388
00:13:15,486 --> 00:13:16,788
The band is already three

389
00:13:16,788 --> 00:13:19,142
quarters of the way around the building.

390
00:13:19,675 --> 00:13:20,993
The only open stretch

391
00:13:20,993 --> 00:13:23,107
is behind the garden yard.

392
00:13:23,107 --> 00:13:24,613
And it's getting shorter.

393
00:13:24,613 --> 00:13:26,732
You have time for one trip.

394
00:13:26,732 --> 00:13:28,034
What you carry.

395
00:13:28,034 --> 00:13:29,010
What stays.

396
00:13:29,010 --> 00:13:31,435
The bottles go in, all of them.

397
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,213
The stove,

398
00:13:32,213 --> 00:13:37,184
the canisters, the tape, the lantern, the map, the tin.

399
00:13:37,783 --> 00:13:38,959
The buckets stay.

400
00:13:38,959 --> 00:13:40,204
So does the tarp,

401
00:13:40,204 --> 00:13:43,217
still hanging where it gave you away.

402
00:13:43,217 --> 00:13:44,284
Mara goes first,

403
00:13:44,284 --> 00:13:46,981
through the gap in the yard fence.

404
00:13:46,981 --> 00:13:49,056
You follow with both hands full.

405
00:13:49,056 --> 00:13:51,519
The light closes in from both sides,

406
00:13:51,519 --> 00:13:53,571
as quiet as spilled water.

407
00:13:54,073 --> 00:13:56,015
You step over the last dark strip of

408
00:13:56,015 --> 00:13:58,546
ground with about a bag's width to spare.

409
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:01,343
Behind you, the two ends of the band meet.

410
00:14:01,343 --> 00:14:02,580
The store is sealed.

411
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:05,569
You don't wait to see which way it opens.

412
00:14:05,569 --> 00:14:06,264
By day 51,

413
00:14:06,264 --> 00:14:09,489
you've walked farther than your map can hold.

414
00:14:09,489 --> 00:14:11,095
You keep drawing anyway,

415
00:14:11,095 --> 00:14:14,117
on the back, around the copied ledger.

416
00:14:14,117 --> 00:14:16,561
Every road you find has units on it.

417
00:14:16,561 --> 00:14:17,767
Every single one.

418
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:20,173
When you have to cross one,

419
00:14:20,173 --> 00:14:22,368
the nearest circles flicker as you pass,

420
00:14:22,368 --> 00:14:25,379
and you don't stop to see whether anything answers.

421
00:14:25,379 --> 00:14:28,383
You spend one night under a bus shelter,

422
00:14:28,383 --> 00:14:30,827
one under a hedge, and one in the rain,

423
00:14:30,827 --> 00:14:33,087
which you would rather not discuss.

424
00:14:33,087 --> 00:14:35,452
Then Mara finds the railway.

425
00:14:35,452 --> 00:14:36,992
A single line of track,

426
00:14:36,992 --> 00:14:39,367
sunk below a row of backyards.

427
00:14:39,774 --> 00:14:41,828
You watch it for half a day.

428
00:14:41,828 --> 00:14:42,536
No units.

429
00:14:42,536 --> 00:14:43,544
No marks.

430
00:14:43,887 --> 00:14:44,625
No lights.

431
00:14:44,625 --> 00:14:47,807
The rails run straight out of the city,

432
00:14:47,807 --> 00:14:49,882
the opposite way from the stadium.

433
00:14:49,882 --> 00:14:51,368
Away from the ship.

434
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:53,836
On day five, when Mara asked where

435
00:14:53,836 --> 00:14:56,798
you would go, that was your whole answer.

436
00:14:56,798 --> 00:14:57,540
It still is.

437
00:14:57,540 --> 00:14:59,452
You walk on the wooden ties,

438
00:14:59,452 --> 00:15:01,004
not the stones between them,

439
00:15:01,004 --> 00:15:04,562
because the stones are loud and they roll under your feet.

440
00:15:04,562 --> 00:15:06,031
You walk early in the morning

441
00:15:06,031 --> 00:15:07,507
and late in the evening,

442
00:15:07,817 --> 00:15:09,930
and rest in the middle of the day.

443
00:15:09,930 --> 00:15:12,410
At a junction, there's a small brick

444
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:15,509
signal hut with a rain barrel under its gutter.

445
00:15:15,509 --> 00:15:16,720
The door is unlocked.

446
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:18,276
It's the first place in fifty

447
00:15:18,276 --> 00:15:20,600
days where nobody has left a mark.

448
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,401
On day 54,

449
00:15:21,401 --> 00:15:24,817
the rain barrel saves you, and costs you.

450
00:15:24,817 --> 00:15:27,805
The water in it is cold and dark.

451
00:15:27,805 --> 00:15:29,146
Boiling it takes the second

452
00:15:29,146 --> 00:15:31,026
canister down to almost nothing.

453
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,369
You do the math on the back of the map.

454
00:15:33,369 --> 00:15:34,690
One full canister.

455
00:15:34,690 --> 00:15:36,569
Whatever is left in this one.

456
00:15:36,569 --> 00:15:38,585
After that, you find water you

457
00:15:38,585 --> 00:15:41,249
don't need to boil, or you stop boiling it,

458
00:15:41,249 --> 00:15:43,259
and neither of those is a plan.

459
00:15:43,259 --> 00:15:45,096
The food is catching up too.

460
00:15:45,096 --> 00:15:45,715
On day seven,

461
00:15:45,715 --> 00:15:48,792
you decided food would last longer than the drinks.

462
00:15:49,133 --> 00:15:49,784
It did.

463
00:15:49,784 --> 00:15:51,247
Just not by much.

464
00:15:51,247 --> 00:15:53,177
In the afternoon,

465
00:15:53,177 --> 00:15:55,559
Mara touches your arm and points.

466
00:15:55,559 --> 00:15:57,516
Back along the track,

467
00:15:57,516 --> 00:16:01,546
where the line curves toward the city, a dark unit is moving.

468
00:16:01,546 --> 00:16:02,583
It glides above the

469
00:16:02,583 --> 00:16:04,086
rails without touching them.

470
00:16:04,086 --> 00:16:05,963
It stops beside the track.

471
00:16:05,963 --> 00:16:07,480
Something lights at its base.

472
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,867
Joined circles.

473
00:16:08,867 --> 00:16:09,711
Then it stays.

474
00:16:09,711 --> 00:16:11,569
They're mapping the railway now.

475
00:16:11,569 --> 00:16:13,297
From the city outward.

476
00:16:13,297 --> 00:16:14,772
From where you came.

477
00:16:14,772 --> 00:16:17,394
On day 57, you push too hard.

478
00:16:17,394 --> 00:16:20,063
The unit has moved twice since day 54,

479
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:22,636
and both times it stopped closer.

480
00:16:22,636 --> 00:16:25,571
So you leave the hut in daylight and walk fast,

481
00:16:25,571 --> 00:16:27,819
on the stones when the ties are wet.

482
00:16:27,819 --> 00:16:29,410
Less than an hour out,

483
00:16:29,410 --> 00:16:32,201
Mara's foot goes sideways on the stones.

484
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:33,970
She doesn't make a sound.

485
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:35,896
That's how you know it's bad.

486
00:16:36,255 --> 00:16:39,190
By evening, her ankle has swollen.

487
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:42,029
You offer her your scarf to wrap it.

488
00:16:42,029 --> 00:16:43,497
She refuses.

489
00:16:43,497 --> 00:16:45,483
She says it's the only thing that

490
00:16:45,483 --> 00:16:47,934
still makes you look like yourself.

491
00:16:47,934 --> 00:16:49,336
You strap the ankle with the

492
00:16:49,336 --> 00:16:51,473
tape from the hardware store instead.

493
00:16:51,911 --> 00:16:52,882
Then you make the

494
00:16:52,882 --> 00:16:54,554
decision you've been dreading.

495
00:16:54,554 --> 00:16:55,663
You turn back.

496
00:16:56,246 --> 00:16:57,756
Two days in the signal hut,

497
00:16:57,756 --> 00:17:00,898
a little closer to the unit than you'd like.

498
00:17:00,898 --> 00:17:01,967
Two days of water,

499
00:17:01,967 --> 00:17:04,806
gas, and distance you can't get back.

500
00:17:04,806 --> 00:17:06,305
You take the first watch,

501
00:17:06,305 --> 00:17:09,289
and the second, and most of the third.

502
00:17:09,289 --> 00:17:10,630
On the second night,

503
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:14,812
a pale line sweeps along the track, far behind you.

504
00:17:14,812 --> 00:17:16,942
It stops where the unit stands.

505
00:17:16,942 --> 00:17:19,239
Then it turns back toward the city.

506
00:17:19,596 --> 00:17:20,945
You write it down,

507
00:17:20,945 --> 00:17:22,721
with one word beside it.

508
00:17:22,721 --> 00:17:24,024
Observed.

509
00:17:24,024 --> 00:17:25,849
You don't sleep much after that.

510
00:17:25,849 --> 00:17:27,634
By the time you leave,

511
00:17:27,634 --> 00:17:30,357
the last full canister isn't full anymore.

512
00:17:30,763 --> 00:17:33,813
Mara insists on carrying her own bag.

513
00:17:33,813 --> 00:17:35,700
You let her, and you walk slower,

514
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,189
so it doesn't look like you're waiting.

515
00:17:38,189 --> 00:17:41,101
On day 60, the light changes.

516
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,910
You notice it first on the rails.

517
00:17:42,910 --> 00:17:44,408
They're shining.

518
00:17:44,408 --> 00:17:45,181
You look up.

519
00:17:45,181 --> 00:17:47,381
For the first time since the evening

520
00:17:47,381 --> 00:17:49,173
you tried to pay for milk,

521
00:17:49,173 --> 00:17:51,628
there's no straight edge in the sky above you.

522
00:17:51,954 --> 00:17:53,450
The ship is behind you.

523
00:17:53,450 --> 00:17:55,630
A dark wall over the city,

524
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:57,628
lying across the horizon.

525
00:17:57,628 --> 00:17:58,626
Mara laughs,

526
00:17:58,626 --> 00:18:01,903
and the laugh turns into something else halfway through,

527
00:18:01,903 --> 00:18:02,909
and you let it.

528
00:18:03,444 --> 00:18:04,245
Sixty days.

529
00:18:04,245 --> 00:18:06,024
Away from the ship.

530
00:18:06,024 --> 00:18:08,733
Mara takes the pencil and draws

531
00:18:08,733 --> 00:18:10,689
one more line on the back of the map.

532
00:18:10,689 --> 00:18:13,879
The place where the sky starts again.

533
00:18:13,879 --> 00:18:15,322
Then you see it.

534
00:18:15,322 --> 00:18:17,051
Fifty steps ahead,

535
00:18:17,051 --> 00:18:18,917
standing between the rails.

536
00:18:18,917 --> 00:18:20,283
A red fuel can.

537
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:21,269
Empty.

538
00:18:21,269 --> 00:18:24,427
You can tell by the way the wind rocks it.

539
00:18:24,427 --> 00:18:26,295
Mara says it isn't the same can.

540
00:18:26,295 --> 00:18:28,701
There are millions of red cans.

541
00:18:28,701 --> 00:18:30,012
You don't answer.

542
00:18:30,012 --> 00:18:32,879
In sixty days, you've only ever seen one.

543
00:18:32,879 --> 00:18:33,658
Beside it,

544
00:18:33,658 --> 00:18:36,973
two circles joined by a short line begin to glow.

545
00:18:36,973 --> 00:18:40,471
Then another pair, farther down the track.

546
00:18:40,471 --> 00:18:41,460
And another.

547
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,153
Leading on, away from the city,

548
00:18:44,153 --> 00:18:47,532
into country neither of you has ever seen.

549
00:18:47,532 --> 00:18:49,135
Mara looks at the can.

550
00:18:49,135 --> 00:18:51,006
Then she looks at you.

551
00:18:51,006 --> 00:18:52,400
Thirty days ago,

552
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:56,379
you had no idea where they expected you to go.

553
00:18:56,379 --> 00:18:57,517
Now you're standing

554
00:18:57,517 --> 00:18:59,686
exactly where they expected you.
